  "behavior": [
    "Private i32 register carriers normalize unannotated integer parameters, returns and ordinary call arguments/results at widths one through sixteen. Explicit masks preserve only defined narrow bits, including direct boolean branches.",
    "Boolean xor uses a private scalar carrier. Existing typed boolean call returns and the specialized intByteSize signature retain their established paths.",
    "Ordinary call preparation reserves preservation storage for instruction-produced arguments even on their last use; existing other barrier policies remain unchanged.",
    "The unchanged canonical Fast capture emits sixteen of thirty-four functions, including the original Fibonacci main function and its six assertion call sites; the first remaining boundary is llvm.umin.i64."
  ],
  "known_boundaries": [
    "Annotated narrow return ABIs, unsupported call envelopes and wider integers retain their existing boundaries.",
    "Frameless wide arithmetic across several zext/shift intermediates retains separate scalar preservation/home limits documented in the focused record.",
    "Fast and Small each select 34 functions and emit 16. ReleaseSafe conservatively selects 1568 and emits 206, with 1362 failures; its LLVM reference link separately requires __zig_probe_stack. No local whole-program execution has succeeded.",
    "The authorized plan continues through stack/aggregate, scalar/memory and indirect-call support, then all-mode unchanged Fibonacci with the original six assertions."
  ],
